  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The current best is config_019 (0.639 acc, multimodal/multiprofile/pca_n2000/resnet50/avgpool/weighted). The image modality contributes ~4.8% over RNA-only but is the weakest component (image-only resnet50 = 0.208). Config_025 makes a single change—replacing resnet50 with the stronger imagenet_vit_l encoder—while keeping all other settings at their known-optimal values (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion). This isolates the effect of image encoder quality on multimodal fusion. If the stronger ViT-L features improve the image branch, the weighted fusion should benefit disproportionately since it can up-weight a more informative image representation. This is the highest-impact single-variable test available: it targets the weakest link in the current best pipeline, and with 2 experiments remaining, a successful result would establish a new best while leaving one experiment for a final refinement (e.g., testing transformer aggregation in config_027)."
}

